```
// Define input parameters
input int	LotSize	= 1;	// Lot size (number of units)
input int	Period	= 50;	// EMA period

// Define variables
double	ema	= 0;	// 50-period EMA
double	lastCandle	= 0;	// Last candle's close price
double	lot	= 0;	// Lot size in units

// On each tick, calculate the EMA and check if the candle has closed above it
if (close > ema)
{
    // Buy the specified lot size
    OrderSend("Buy", LotSize, market, 100000);

    // Update the last candle's close price for the next tick
    lastCandle = close;

    // Update the EMA
    ema = average(close, Period);
}
```
Note: This EA uses the `OrderSend` function to send a market order to buy the specified lot size. It does not include any stop loss or profit taking rules, so it is important to carefully test and evaluate the EA's performance before using it in a live trading environment.

